Subject: [PATCH] J714s release 10: kernel v272-19 and firmware j714s15

Re-pinned from betizzel/omarchy-m5:
- linux-aurora 7.3.0.aurora17.v272-19 (7ddee362..., 44635498 bytes) from
  731670d: aurora-silicon/linux main 0c1f7e707784 plus
  patches/j714s-27.2/linux 0001-0011 (re-pinned; this week's T6050 sleep
  series, DP pin D, upstream camera tuning #2233). CONFIG_APPLE_SOC_SLEEP
  stays off. Built on the build host (x86_64 cross, clang 23.1.5, Rust
  1.98.1). The qualification pins follow 7.3.0-17.v272-19-ARCH.
- omarchy-aurora-firmware 20261014.j714s15 from 5acbae7: no VRR drop-in
  (aurora-m5-vrr.conf), VRR crashed the K114s DCP (betizzel/omarchy-m5#25).
  The aarch64 .pkg.tar.xz (ccfae7a9...) recompressed to zstd with the same
  tar inside (d99d4dd9...), 2f9493dd..., 53899 bytes.
Nothing else changes. Set j714s-dev-runtime-1438d54ecdd3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
